id: entrusted
name: Entrusted
kind: state
description: >
  Everything your allies had, you are carrying.
text: >
  (1) [Passive]: Apply your Greater Dice to your Combat Rolls.

  (2) [Passive]: Increase your Stress Bonus by 1.

  (3) [Triggered/Entrusted]: Gain 1 Action.

  (4) [Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you would use the Basic Attack Maneuver, you
  may apply the Full Wager Advantage and All-or-Nothing Disadvantage to that
  Attacking Maneuver. If you do, reset your Capacity to your Max Capacity before
  using this Attacking Maneuver and then leave the Entrusted Special State after
  concluding that Attacking Maneuver.

---

# (1) and (2) are here and are the whole of themselves. (3) and (4) are not:
#
#   - (4) hangs two Signature features onto a Basic Attack that is not a Signature
#     Technique, refills Capacity first and leaves the State afterwards. The two
#     features exist now; what does not is a way to put them on an attack that did
#     not declare them, or to refill Capacity, which is spent rather than set.

# (1) and (2). The Greater Dice line is the same one Superior uses, and the same Slot.
[passive]
combatRolls.dice += greaterDice;
stressBonus += 1;

# (3). "Gain 1 Action" - one more until your turn ends, which is what an Action is
# worth: they are handed back when the round turns over anyway, so an Action that
# outlived your turn would be an Action nobody could spend.
#
# Written as unspending one rather than as raising the round's allowance, because that
# is what "gain" means here - what is held is how many you spent, and what is left is
# the allowance less that.
[triggered/state/entrusted]
actions.remaining += 1;
